# Env files carry SERPER_API_KEY. Ignore every .env.dspark variant
# (.text-0731, .vision-exp, ...) but keep the committed example.
.env.dspark
.env.dspark.*
!.env.dspark.example
.env
.secrets/
*.pem
*.key
id_*
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.log
vllm-cache/
/models/
# --- local-ops/ : track the TOOLING, never what it captures -----------------
# The scripts here are part of how this cluster is operated and debugged, so
# they belong in the repo — keeping them out is what left the only copy of
# verify-server.py on one laptop.
#
# What they PRODUCE stays out: prompt captures contain full conversations and
# are sensitive, and the result sets are large (54 MB of toolsearch-matrix
# captures alone, against 444 KB of actual tooling).
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT, then allow, and deliberately so: a new capture or log format
# is ignored automatically, while a new script has to be added on purpose. The
# reverse (ignore *.log, *.jsonl, ...) fails open the first time something
# writes a format nobody listed.
/local-ops/**
!/local-ops/**/
!/local-ops/**/*.py
!/local-ops/**/*.sh
!/local-ops/**/*.md
!/local-ops/**/requirements.txt
!/local-ops/dspark-dropcaches
!/local-ops/dspark-dmesg
# user systemd units (spark-memwatch, engine-supervisor) -- tooling, not output
!/local-ops/systemd/*.service
# the semantic canary's FIXED prompt and sentinel (sha-pinned in kvcanary.py)
!/local-ops/kvcanary/*.txt

# ONE named .json, and it is CONFIGURATION rather than a capture.
# flags.reference.json is the committed source for /var/tmp/vllm-kv-flags/flags.json,
# the boot-time default for every policy knob -- which is per node, unversioned,
# and was found diverged between the two nodes (head 12 keys Oct 10, worker 9
# keys Oct 7, disagreeing about disk_restore). Versioning it is the whole point.
#
# Deliberately a SINGLE PATH and not `*.json`: the deny-by-default above exists
# because captures are json/jsonl and contain full conversations, so a pattern
# here would fail open exactly the way the comment above warns about. A second
# config file gets a second line.
!/local-ops/flags.reference.json

# ...except these, which are DATA that happens to be .py/.md:
#   baseline-20260914/  unpatched vLLM source + a rollback snapshot. patches/
#                       pristine/ is the tracked source of truth for that now,
#                       and two files here are byte-identical to it.
#   xsess/image-src/    more copies of vLLM source, pulled during an investigation.
#   rollback/           head-only copies of our own scripts, by definition stale.
/local-ops/baseline-20260914/
/local-ops/xsess/image-src/
/local-ops/rollback/
